.TH "HED-AUTOSAVE" "1" "2026-08-20" "hed v1.21.1" "hed manual"
.SH NAME
hed\-autosave \- Idle / timer autosave for dirty buffers, with a
recovery prompt on reopen.
Crash\-safe \[em] the editor cache survives a kill \-9 or a power loss
without overwriting your real source files until you :w.
.PP
Idle / timer autosave for dirty buffers, with a recovery prompt on
reopen.
Crash\-safe \[em] the editor cache survives a kill \-9 or a power loss
without overwriting your real source files until you \f[CR]:w\f[R].
.SH Layout
For an editor cwd of \f[CR]/mnt/storage/probe/hed\f[R] and a buffer
named \f[CR]src/foo.c\f[R], the autosave file lives at:
.IP
.EX
\[ti]/.cache/hed/%mnt%storage%probe%hed/autosave/src/foo.c
.EE
.PP
\[em] same per\-cwd cache dir the editor log uses, with the original
relative path mirrored under \f[CR]autosave/\f[R].
Easy to grep, easy to wipe (\f[CR]rm \-rf\f[R] the cwd\[cq]s cache dir).
.PP
Writes are atomic: \f[CR]<path>.tmp\f[R] is created,
\f[CR]fsync\f[R]\[cq]d, then renamed over the target.
A crash mid\-write leaves no half\-written autosave.
.SH Cadence
Two triggers:
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]3 seconds of idleness\f[R] after the last keystroke
(\f[CR]HOOK_CHAR_INSERT\f[R] / \f[CR]HOOK_CHAR_DELETE\f[R] schedule a
debounced timer; further edits reset it).
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]Every transition out of INSERT mode\f[R] (\f[CR]<Esc>\f[R] from
insert flushes immediately).
.PP
Tunable today only by editing \f[CR]AUTOSAVE_IDLE_MS\f[R] in
\f[CR]autosave.c\f[R] and rebuilding.
.SH Recovery
When a buffer opens (\f[CR]HOOK_BUFFER_OPEN\f[R]), the plugin checks
whether a fresh autosave exists.
\[lq]Fresh\[rq] means: the autosave file\[cq]s mtime is strictly newer
than the on\-disk file\[cq]s mtime.
If yes, the user is prompted via the shared \f[CR]ask\f[R] helper:
.IP
.EX
autosave found for src/foo.c \[em] restore? (y/n) y
.EE
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[CR]y\f[R] / \f[CR]Y\f[R] (or just Enter, since \f[CR]\[dq]y\[dq]\f[R]
is the default) replaces the buffer\[cq]s rows with the autosave
contents and marks the buffer dirty (\f[CR]buf\->dirty = 1\f[R]).
You still have to \f[CR]:w\f[R] to commit.
.IP \[bu] 2
Anything else discards the autosave silently.
.PP
Stale autosaves (where the on\-disk file is at least as new) are deleted
without prompting \[em] they can\[cq]t tell you anything you don\[cq]t
already have.
.PP
The undo stack is dropped on restore.
Otherwise undo would walk the buffer through ghost edits that never
actually happened in this session, which is more confusing than helpful.
.PP
If a prompt is already open when the file opens (multiple files on the
cli, the recovery prompt for the first is still up), the rest fall back
to a status message and you can re\-prompt with
\f[CR]:autosave restore\f[R].
.SH On \f[CR]:w\f[R]
\f[CR]HOOK_BUFFER_SAVE\f[R] unlinks the autosave file, so a successful
save returns the buffer to a state with no autosave to recover.
.SH Skips
.IP \[bu] 2
Buffers without a filename.
.IP \[bu] 2
Read\-only buffers.
.IP \[bu] 2
Plugin scratch buffers (titles starting with \f[CR][\f[R] \[em]
\f[CR][copilot]\f[R], \f[CR][scratch]\f[R], \f[CR][claude]\f[R], \&...).
.IP \[bu] 2
Files larger than 10 MB (\f[CR]AUTOSAVE_MAX_BYTES\f[R]).
Big logs and binary blobs would otherwise generate a lot of disk traffic
for no recovery benefit.
.SH Commands
.IP
.EX
:autosave                  status (alias for :autosave status)
:autosave on               enable autosave
:autosave off              disable + cancel pending timer
:autosave toggle
:autosave status           show enabled / idle ms / size cap
:autosave restore          re\-prompt the recovery dialog for the
                           current buffer (use after the auto\-prompt
                           was suppressed by another open prompt)
:autosave now              flush every dirty buffer immediately
.EE
.PP
Defaults to \f[B]on\f[R].
To start with autosave off, edit \f[CR]src/config.c\f[R] and pass
\f[CR]0\f[R] instead of \f[CR]1\f[R] to
\f[CR]plugin_load(&plugin_autosave, \&...)\f[R].
.SH Implementation notes
.IP \[bu] 2
Single source file (\f[CR]autosave.c\f[R], \[ti]300 lines).
Uses \f[CR]path_cache_file_for_cwd()\f[R] for the base directory,
\f[CR]path_mkdir_p\f[R] for intermediate dirs, and
\f[CR]ed_loop_timer_after(\[dq]autosave:idle\[dq],   \&...)\f[R] for the
debounced timer (rename\-replaces\-prior semantics give free debounce).
.IP \[bu] 2
The recovery prompt is built on \f[CR]src/ui/ask.h\f[R], the shared
one\-line prompt helper.
The callback parses the answer; the plugin makes no policy beyond
\[lq]starts with y or Y means yes.\[rq]
